  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-27 decision D-234 (notes/decisions.md) on #3283. Read gh issue view 3283, DI-180, D-231 and the #3277 reviews (task 226 notes). The Decision Records tab (SignalReadService Decided set, set=decided) reads two bounded sets: Signal-backed records and email-gate records joined to their email. Add Record Procedure decisions (resolvedSignalIds always empty), billing decisions written with no Signal, and assign-firm decisions: each listed under its core record (matter or project) with its summary and no Open action, exactly as gate records are shown. Each kind gets its own bounded, caller-trimmed read (the caller's identity; never app-only), with the same cap and truncation signal the existing reads use. Writers: DecisionRecordWriter (Procedure ~:2213, billing ~:1764), BillingDecisionRecorder (Services/Finance), the assign-firm path. Search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, the ontology Signal read routes.</role>
  <goal>The Decision Records tab lists every writer-authored Decision Record the caller can read in the window, including Procedure, billing and assign-firm records with no Signal, without bringing back the capped-read 503.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Identify each kind by a stored, writer-trusted property (WriterCreatedRecord, D-145a/task 223), not by text. Keep the window and cap semantics of the existing reads; merge and order the sets as the tab already does; do not duplicate a record that is also Signal-backed. If the client needs a new group label, keep it inside the existing Decision Records tab component (no new component). Run /conflict-check; read git log -5 on the files you edit.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
  </constraints>
